-- Small faulted deck for the live Python API test
-- test_blackoil_fault_faces_only_in_nnc_rates (python/test/test_time_stepping_api.py).
--
-- Derived from SPE1CASE1 (same phases, PVT and units) so that the three-phase
-- BlackOilSimulator runs it. Grid 6 x 4 x 3, uniform DX = DY = 200 ft, DZ = 20 ft.
--
-- Two faults, made by shifting TOPS (vertical pillars, so a shifted column is a fault):
--   * I fault, throw of exactly one layer (20 ft): columns I = 3-4 (one-based) lie 20 ft
--     deeper than columns I = 1-2 and 5-6.
--       - Low-I edge (I = 2 | I = 3): cell (2, J, K) touches only (3, J, K-1) and shares no
--         face with its Cartesian I+ neighbour (3, J, K). The NNC pair has the deeper-column
--         cell (3, J, K-1) as nnc1, i.e. (2, J, K) is the cell2 end of a pair lying on its
--         + side.
--       - High-I edge (I = 4 | I = 5): cell (4, J, K) touches (5, J, K+1), nnc1 is the
--         lower-I cell.
--   * J fault, throw of half a layer (10 ft): rows J = 3-4 lie 10 ft deeper than rows
--     J = 1-2. Cell (I, 2, K) shares half a face with its Cartesian J+ neighbour (I, 3, K)
--     (a regular TRANY connection) and half a face with (I, 3, K-1) (an NNC) on the same
--     side.
--
-- Water is mobile everywhere: the initial state is enumerated (SWAT 0.4 above the connate
-- 0.2 of the SWOF table, so krw > 0 in every cell), and a water injector in the corner
-- (1, 1) drives water towards a liquid producer in the opposite corner (6, 4), across both
-- faults.

RUNSPEC

TITLE
   FAULT NNC - live face-rate rule

DIMENS
   6 4 3 /

TABDIMS
/

OIL
GAS
WATER
DISGAS

FIELD

START
   1 'JAN' 2015 /

WELLDIMS
   2 3 1 2 /

UNIFOUT

GRID

INIT

DX
   72*200 /
DY
   72*200 /
DZ
   72*20 /

-- Top of layer 1 only; the lower layers follow from DZ. Rows J = 1-2 then J = 3-4
-- (+10 ft, the J fault); columns I = 3-4 are +20 ft (the I fault).
TOPS
   8325 8325 8345 8345 8325 8325
   8325 8325 8345 8345 8325 8325
   8335 8335 8355 8355 8335 8335
   8335 8335 8355 8355 8335 8335 /

PORO
   72*0.3 /

PERMX
   72*200 /
PERMY
   72*200 /
PERMZ
   72*20 /

PROPS

PVTW
   4017.55 1.038 3.22E-6 0.318 0.0 /

ROCK
   14.7 3E-6 /

-- Corey water/oil curves, connate water 0.2 and residual oil 0.2: krw > 0 above Sw = 0.2.
SWOF
